# Iterative Binary Search ::

## Problem Statement :
Find the key from a sorted array , using loop. If key is there then return the index , else we have to retun -1.

## Approach : 
1. `low = 0`, `high = n-1`.
2. till then `low <= high`: `mid = low + (high - low) / 2`.
3. `arr[mid] == key` -> found . `arr[mid] < key` -> right half (`low = mid+1`). or left half (`high = mid-1`).
4. Loop ends then there's no element .

## Pseudocode :-
BINARY_SEARCH_ITERATIVE(arr, n, key):
    low = 0
    high = n - 1
    while low <= high:
        mid = low + (high - low) / 2
        if arr[mid] == key: return mid
        else if arr[mid] < key: low = mid + 1
        else: high = mid - 1
    return -1

## Flowchart :-

flowchart TD
    A([Start]) --> B[/Input sorted arr, key/]
    B --> C[low = 0, high = n-1]
    C --> D{low <= high?}
    D -- No --> N[Return -1: Not found] --> Z([End])
    D -- Yes --> E[mid = low + high-low / 2]
    E --> F{arr mid == key?}
    F -- Yes --> G[Return mid: Found] --> Z
    F -- No --> H{arr mid < key?}
    H -- Yes --> I[low = mid + 1] --> D
    H -- No --> J[high = mid - 1] --> D


## Time & Space Complexity
| Case | Time |
|---|---|
| Best | O(1) |
| Average | O(log n) |
| Worst | O(log n) |
| **Space** | **O(1)** |

Har step me search space aadha ho jata hai: n -> n/2 -> n/4 ... -> 1, so ~log2(n) steps.
